\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.9}{\ignorespaces Double descent. To the left of the interpolation threshold, test error follows the U shape of Figure~\ref {fig:05-biasvar}. Near the threshold the model can fit the training data exactly, and test error peaks. Beyond it, among the many models that fit the training data exactly, estimation picks the one with the smallest coefficients, and test error can fall again. The curve is stylized; whether the second descent appears, and how far it falls, depends on the problem.}}{85}{figure.caption.34}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:21-doubledescent}{{5.9}{85}{Double descent. To the left of the interpolation threshold, test error follows the U shape of Figure~\ref {fig:05-biasvar}. Near the threshold the model can fit the training data exactly, and test error peaks. Beyond it, among the many models that fit the training data exactly, estimation picks the one with the smallest coefficients, and test error can fall again. The curve is stylized; whether the second descent appears, and how far it falls, depends on the problem}{figure.caption.34}{}}
